# Kernel module build output. NEVER commit these: vermagic ties a .ko to one kernel release, and a checkout
# with fresh timestamps can make `make` skip the rebuild and ship a STALE module that silently does not match
# the guest kernel. Build it from appidmod.c with the Makefile here, which targets the GUEST kernel release
# from ../../m1/domain.env.
*.ko
*.o
*.mod
*.mod.c
*.cmd
.*.cmd
Module.symvers
modules.order
.module-common.o
